Short and to the point: I have no idea, sorry. You are the trailblazer in using rhdfs with foreach as far as I know.
Larger unrequested point: how could this approach possibly scale in any way? Why do you bother with hdfs in the first place? If you are going to read the data into main memory, that caps it at a few GBs. Doesn't seem a natural application of hdfs when a thumb drive would do. If you considered rmr2, this is no replacement.  Even if you had unlimited memory, you'd be taxing a single network link, what is the point? If the files are small, read it one at a time and then do whatever calculations you need in parallel. Sorry if I am missing something.

Antonio

