In-Reply-To: <YXLo2zjaw8I.25wL1mbUva0J@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
References: <YXLo2zjaw8I.25wL1mbUva0J@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/YXLo2zjaw8I/m/CWS1WZZovNMJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,
I tried this before and gave up. The console output can be captured in R (see last few lines of function rmr2:::rmr.stream, when option verbose is FALSE it is actually captured) but becomes available only when the system call returns, that is the job is done. That's by definition too late to kill the job. If anyone knows of a mechanism to make this work, that's always been my goal: on exit mapreduce should do a complete cleanup, including terminating a job if the function is not allowed to wait for its termination (abnormal exit).

Antonio

