Hi
I would recommend a hadoop mapreduce tutorial first to  answer questions about data and compute load distribution and then the RHadoop wiki to see how this is made available in R. For mahout questions, this is not the best venue but there are dedicated forums. Also the r-project.org <http://r-project.org> HPC view could be of interest to you. Algorithms must be implemented to take advantage of the rmr2 API or  there is no advantage in loading the package. I think this is true of most parallel libraries for Hadoop and beyond, automatic parallelization is not something that anybody expects to become a common, general answer to performance issues in the foreseeable future.

Antonio

